# Everything below stays OUT of the Docker build context. The context is what a build daemon (possibly a remote one) receives, so the
# owner's private evidence, credentials and local artifacts must never be in it. scripts/deploy-safety.mjs checks these rules against
# planted canaries; do not weaken them without updating that check.

# --- private by nature -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/private
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.artifacts
**/.cache
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/.git
**/.runtime
**/.venv
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
**/*.log
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*

# --- regenerated inside the image --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- not needed to build or run ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests
docs
deploy
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.gitattributes
AGENTS.md
TasteGate_AI_Qloo_Hackathon_Prize_Strategy_*.md
